{"id": "EUVD-2026-86820", "enisaUuid": "eeb3d436-1a1e-33b2-a5ae-8350bab5728a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nocteontx2-pf: reset HTB scheduler topology before freeing queues\n\nHTB offload programs NIX_AF_TLxX_TOPOLOGY on QoS-allocated scheduler\nqueues via otx2_qos_txschq_set_parent_topology(), but teardown freed\nthose queues without clearing TOPOLOGY.  The AF only restores PARENT and\nSCHEDULE on free, so PRIO_ANCHOR/RR_PRIO settings can survive in the\nshared scheduler pool and affect later allocations.\n\nAdd otx2_qos_reset_schq_topology() and otx2_qos_free_hw_schq() to zero\nTL4 through TL2 TOPOLOGY before each schq is returned to the AF during\nhierarchy teardown and cfg rollback.  Skip the aggregation level (TL1):\nit is a per-tx-link queue shared by the PF, default Tx hierarchy and VFs,\nand is not freed back to the AF by nix_txschq_free_one().", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:23:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:11:32", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/16c5c8ea5017952ff14c87626a45359d195dda6f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0aa2dd6eaa347c7aab448df0eec0afcfe7489885", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/621c99be42e3f5cb68a6af9480a255218a761c4e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2df186418e17b30b319cf9ff81aad137692ab107", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ef39fca8508597fa565cf2be72a884a712fb98af"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97966", "GHSA-m5mf-8q2j-8cgp"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "20e46ce3-4780-397a-b5aa-abbb9df4ec59", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5e6808b4c68d7882971514ab3279926eb07c8b2d <0aa2dd6eaa347c7aab448df0eec0afcfe7489885"}, {"id": "3316d352-110c-39c0-9133-e1267db00e38", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "52627d74-7a5a-3d50-b5f7-1af82d03f859", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "54650e7a-b64e-33ef-884f-2805e914e678", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5e6808b4c68d7882971514ab3279926eb07c8b2d <2df186418e17b30b319cf9ff81aad137692ab107"}, {"id": "6ca0dcfd-073d-3ed5-a490-d2a6e6ae872a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5e6808b4c68d7882971514ab3279926eb07c8b2d <621c99be42e3f5cb68a6af9480a255218a761c4e"}, {"id": "8d911cf1-44d3-3172-bd0b-3a224180f72b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5e6808b4c68d7882971514ab3279926eb07c8b2d <ef39fca8508597fa565cf2be72a884a712fb98af"}, {"id": "9442cd2f-b015-36b1-ba3c-440620e8b95f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "9de9fd09-3a2f-37a7-8b7a-e80f5d1cf601", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5e6808b4c68d7882971514ab3279926eb07c8b2d <16c5c8ea5017952ff14c87626a45359d195dda6f"}, {"id": "c3af0eaf-41c7-3e02-896d-3de38144b75d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.5"}, {"id": "c9e76ce1-66b4-36c4-ad7d-233c65f120bd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "e14939e3-564a-3514-a215-b3ad2931dceb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "e2b72545-3283-3121-b317-96d4b8ea1ddd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f17ff42c-2e28-3ba0-9613-e7fcecd0f9c2", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}